    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0379" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg287"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 781.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith, for your information
                    and the embassy files, copy of a memorandum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d243-f1"/>
                    furnished to this Department by the German embassy stating the intention of the
                    German Government to send two officials to the United States to confer with the
                    presidents of the Equitable, the New York, and the Mutual Life Insurance
                    companies with a view to reaching an arrangement by which these companies may be
                    enabled to resume business in Prussia.</p>
                <p>I have communicated this information to the presidents of the three companies
                    named.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
